        "explanation": "The mathematics of partial emancipation followed directly from Virginia inheritance law. The 123 Washington owned outright could be bequeathed; he freed them via his July 1799 will (accelerated by Martha to January 1, 1801). The 153 Custis dower slaves were trust property — Martha held only a life interest, and they passed to her four grandchildren in 1802. The 41 Mercer slaves were leased and went back to that estate. None of the 194 received freedom in their lifetimes. Knowing this structure is essential to understanding both the moral seriousness and the structural limits of Washington's will.",
